---
import Layout from '../layouts/WorkspaceLayout.astro'
import { WORKSPACE_VERSION, WORKSPACE_DOWNLOAD_URL, WORKSPACE_RELEASE_URL, WORKSPACE_SOURCE_URL, WORKSPACE_CHECKSUMS_URL, WORKSPACE_SHA256 } from '../lib/workspace-release.mjs'
const prepareCommand = `uv sync --frozen --no-dev --project /absolute/path/to/veqtor-workspace-${WORKSPACE_VERSION}`
const connectionTimeouts = 'startup_timeout_sec = 180\ntool_timeout_sec = 330'
const firstPrompt = 'Use Veqtor Workspace to open the Word file at [paste the file location here]. Add a comment saying "Reviewed with Veqtor Workspace." Attach it to the first paragraph with text. Keep the document text unchanged. Save the result as a new file in the same folder, then tell me where it is.'
const launchCommand = `uv run --frozen --no-dev --project /absolute/path/to/veqtor-workspace-${WORKSPACE_VERSION} veqtor-workspace --author "Your Name"`
const launchArguments = `run\n--frozen\n--no-dev\n--project\n/absolute/path/to/veqtor-workspace-${WORKSPACE_VERSION}\nveqtor-workspace\n--author\nYour Name`
---
<Layout canonicalPath="/setup" title="Get started — Veqtor Workspace" description="Connect Veqtor Workspace to Claude Desktop or ChatGPT Desktop on your Mac. Try a small edit on a copy of a Word document.">
  <div class="shell setup-heading"><p class="concept-kicker">Installation</p><h1>Start with your AI assistant.</h1><p class="section-intro">Connect Veqtor on your Mac, then try one small change on a copy of a Word file.</p></div>
  <div class="shell setup-container" data-tabs>
    <div class="example-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Choose your assistant"><button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-claude" aria-controls="panel-claude" aria-selected="true">Claude Desktop</button><button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-chatgpt" aria-controls="panel-chatgpt" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">ChatGPT Desktop</button></div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="panel-claude" aria-labelledby="tab-claude">
      <section class="setup-step"><span>1</span><div><h2>Download Veqtor for Mac</h2><p>You’ll need <a href="https://claude.com/download">Claude Desktop</a> installed and signed in. Download the extension for your Mac.</p><a class="concept-button primary" href={WORKSPACE_DOWNLOAD_URL}>Download for Claude Desktop <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><p class="example-note">Version {WORKSPACE_VERSION} · Apple Silicon and Intel · <a href={WORKSPACE_RELEASE_URL}>Release notes</a></p><details class="setup-details"><summary>Verify the download</summary><p>The <a href={WORKSPACE_CHECKSUMS_URL}>release checksums</a> identify the published installer. Its SHA-256 is:</p><div class="copy-container"><div class="copy-heading"><span>SHA-256</span><span data-copy-status role="status"></span><button type="button" data-copy="installer-checksum">Copy</button></div><pre id="installer-checksum">{WORKSPACE_SHA256}</pre></div></details></div></section>
      <section class="setup-step"><span>2</span><div><h2>Open it in Claude Desktop</h2><p>Open the downloaded file with Claude Desktop and choose Install. Enter the name you want used for new tracked changes and comments, then enable Veqtor Workspace.</p><p>No terminal commands or separate Python installation are needed. The first start downloads the required runtime and libraries; let it finish, then open a new chat.</p><p>Ask Claude whether it can see the Veqtor Workspace tools.</p></div></section>
      <section class="setup-step"><span>3</span><div><h2>Point to a saved copy</h2><p>Make a copy of a Word file with sample text. Save and close it in Word. In Finder, select the copy and press <kbd>⌥ ⌘ C</kbd> to copy its full location.</p><p>Paste that location into the request below. Veqtor uses the files you identify in your request.</p></div></section>
    </div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="panel-chatgpt" aria-labelledby="tab-chatgpt" hidden>
      <section class="setup-step"><span>1</span><div><h2>Prepare the desktop app</h2><p>Use ChatGPT Desktop on your Mac with local work enabled. This connection needs <a href="https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/">uv</a> and the Workspace source folder. Download the folder below, unzip it and keep it in a permanent location.</p><a class="concept-button" href={WORKSPACE_SOURCE_URL}>Download Workspace source <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><p class="example-note">Version {WORKSPACE_VERSION}. This is a manual setup for local chats in the desktop app. The Claude extension above is for Claude Desktop.</p><details class="setup-details"><summary>Prepare the downloaded folder</summary><p>After installing uv, run this once in Terminal. Replace the example location with your downloaded folder. Wait until it finishes before adding the connection.</p><div class="copy-container"><div class="copy-heading"><span>First-time preparation</span><span data-copy-status role="status"></span><button type="button" data-copy="prepare-command">Copy</button></div><pre id="prepare-command">{prepareCommand}</pre></div></details></div></section>
      <section class="setup-step"><span>2</span><div><h2>Connect Veqtor in Settings</h2><p>Open Settings → MCP servers → Add server. Name it “Veqtor Workspace”, choose STDIO, and enter the connection settings below. Save, then restart the connection.</p><details class="setup-details"><summary>Show connection settings</summary><p>Set the command to <code>uv</code>. Add the following arguments, one per entry. Replace the folder location and “Your Name” with your own.</p><div class="copy-container"><div class="copy-heading"><span>Arguments · one per line</span><span data-copy-status role="status"></span><button type="button" data-copy="launch-arguments">Copy</button></div><pre id="launch-arguments">{launchArguments}</pre></div><p>If the app cannot find uv, use its full location as the command. See <a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/extend/mcp?surface=cli">OpenAI’s connection instructions</a> for the current setup options.</p><p>In this server’s section of <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>, add these settings so startup and longer document tasks have time to finish:</p><div class="copy-container"><div class="copy-heading"><span>Connection timeouts</span><span data-copy-status role="status"></span><button type="button" data-copy="connection-timeouts">Copy</button></div><pre id="connection-timeouts">{connectionTimeouts}</pre></div></details><details class="setup-details"><summary>Using Codex CLI or the IDE extension?</summary><p>The local server also works with Codex. Add it using the same command and arguments:</p><div class="copy-container"><div class="copy-heading"><span>Local launch command</span><span data-copy-status role="status"></span><button type="button" data-copy="launch-command">Copy</button></div><pre id="launch-command">{launchCommand}</pre></div></details></div></section>
      <section class="setup-step"><span>3</span><div><h2>Start with a copy of a document</h2><p>Make a copy of a Word file with sample text. Save and close it. In Finder, select the copy and press <kbd>⌥ ⌘ C</kbd> to copy its full location.</p><p>Start a new chat, check that Veqtor Workspace is connected, and paste the file location into your request.</p></div></section>
    </div>
    <section class="setup-step"><span>4</span><div><h2>Add your first comment</h2><p>Replace the bracketed text with the file’s location. This request adds one comment and saves a new file.</p><div class="copy-container"><div class="copy-heading"><span>Your first request</span><span data-copy-status role="status"></span><button type="button" data-copy="first-prompt">Copy request</button></div><blockquote id="first-prompt">{firstPrompt}</blockquote></div><p>Open the result in Word and check the comment and the document. For your next text edit, ask for tracked changes if you want to review each change.</p></div></section>
    <div class="setup-trouble"><h3>Before your first task</h3><div class="questions"><details><summary>What if Claude cannot install the extension?</summary><p>Use the current Claude Desktop app and open the downloaded file with it. If your organization restricts custom extensions, ask its administrator to allow Veqtor Workspace.</p></details><details><summary>I already use Veqtor MCP. Is this the same installer?</summary><p>Workspace is a separate product. The earlier installer and documentation remain available on the <a href="/veqtor-mcp">Veqtor MCP 0.5 page</a>. An existing Workspace preview updates in place when you install this extension.</p></details><details><summary>Can I keep editing in Word while the assistant works?</summary><p>Save first, and avoid editing the same file while the assistant saves it. Veqtor cannot read unsaved Word changes. If it updates a file that is still open in Word, reopen that file before continuing your manual edits.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need to write code?</summary><p>You describe the document task in normal language. Claude Desktop uses an extension; the current ChatGPT Desktop setup requires a manual local connection. The document work itself does not require you to write code.</p></details><details><summary>Can I use confidential documents?</summary><p>Veqtor runs locally, but document content returned to the assistant becomes part of your AI conversation. Use documents only when processing them with your chosen AI service is permitted. Start with sample text.</p></details></div></div>
  </div>
</Layout>
